experiment: switchrate
  the question      §55. §54 imposed wrong writes in TRIAL-LENGTH blocks (the pin
                    is set once per window) and found AVERAGING. Short runs are
                    the one candidate left for the derived index's 3.3-4.0 SE
                    deficit, and its run length has NEVER been measured.
  the quantity      runlen = sum(live) / (sum(switches) + windows), in ticks. A
                    SWITCH is a live tick whose slot differs from the previous
                    LIVE tick's. Pooled as a ratio of sums, not a mean of
                    per-window ratios (`mean-of-ratios`).
  the boundaries    A: CI lower >= 450 (<=1 switch/window) -- short runs REFUTED.
                    B: CI upper <= 150 (the feedback period) -- SURVIVES.
                    C: anything else, including a straddling CI. The estimator's
                    ceiling is 900 ticks by construction.
  session           450.0 s of simulated life x 84 sessions, 6 arms
  instrument        switchrate   trial seed 0000000001357269   84 sessions
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)

